R-I5 R-I6 R-H1 R-H2 R-H3 R-H4 R-H6 R-C1 R-C6 R-C7 R-C9 R-RP3 R-DI15 R-SP21 R-NS5 R-AL1 R-AL3 R-AL7 R-VA1 R-SP18 R-PH11 R-NS11: install with a key of talon.toml that the header does not have (the npm-like add).
Run 1: the header gets the highest release of acme/parser that min-release-age and R-C6 allow (1.2.0: 1.3.0 is a prerelease, 1.4.0 a draft) as a new entry after the last one, and the roc pin of the compiler as the last entry (R-RP3). The other bytes stay: the platform keyword, the comments, the spacing, the path entry local (R-H4) and the foreign URL other (R-H4). The comma after the old last entry is the form of roc-app-header add_entry. The index is fetched once, the packages of the header and of the new release are read from the cache (no download). Run 2: the key is now an entry: nothing to change.
